{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455764-mars-terraforming-versus-human-genetic-engineering","id":1455764,"title":"Mars, terraforming versus human genetic engineering","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-29T14:35:29-07:00","id":1455764,"title":"Mars, terraforming versus human genetic engineering","content":"If colonizing Mars is possible, more so in a universe of Magick, a choice presents itself between two methods. Somehow less controversial is the idea of completely transforming the planet to suit humans as we are, a mega-industrial project. The one that makes the masses go, &quot;Ick!&quot;, is the idea of genetically engineering a species of humans who are adapted to the conditions there. In Mage society, which method would each individual Convention and Tradition favor? Which would oppose the adventure in any form?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-29T15:31:53-07:00","id":1455765,"title":"","content":"Are we assuming that Mars is, as the technocracy would have us believe, an uninhabitable rocky planet and not the shard realm of the sphere of forces?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24383-laughinggull","name":"LaughingGull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24383_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-29T15:35:42-07:00","id":1455766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455764-mars-terraforming-versus-human-genetic-engineering#post1455764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If colonizing Mars is possible, more so in a universe of Magick, a choice presents itself between two methods. Somehow less controversial is the idea of completely transforming the planet to suit humans as we are, a mega-industrial project. The one that makes the masses go, &quot;Ick!&quot;, is the idea of genetically engineering a species of humans who are adapted to the conditions there. In Mage society, which method would each individual Convention and Tradition favor? Which would oppose the adventure in any form?</div> </div> </div> </div>My thoughts on the matter at the moment:<br /> <br /> - Progenitors would definitely favor the &quot;adapting people to the enviroment&quot; path, though experimenting with self-sustaining enviromental changes through the use of mutated bacterial and/or fungal (among other organisms) might also be an option.<br /> <br /> - Syndicate might favor or oppose it depending if they want the more economically practical or an astronomically costly and neverending undertaking that might assure the jobs of countless peoples for generations - in fact these and more could lead to something on a broken base on the issue.<br /> <br /> - Iteration X views might be similar to those of Progenitors in prefering to tailor the people to the enviroment - through cybernetics in their case, obviously, what should lead to competition with the Progenitors over what method is more suited to the situation, practical to the Conventions resources and so on.<br /> <br /> - The Void Engineers might either accept any support as long as it gets the boat forward - or have some specific knowledge of conditions, natural &amp; supernatural, in the red planet, that makes them opposed to the idea of &quot;geo\u200bformatting&quot; as a whole. So, an ironic broken base potential much like with the Syndicate, i guess.<br /> <br /> - NWO.... no idea whatsoever, really.<br /> <br /> <br /> About the Traditions going to Mars.... honestly, i don't see anyone beside the Etherites having an interest on this as a group. Too far from their respective paradigms and arenas.<br /> <br /> Correction - Dreamspeakers, Akashics, Choristers, Batinni and others with some interest in out-of-body experiences and spiritual vision quests might involve themselves with astral journeys in other worlds, what might led, if not to attempts at colonization, at least a degree of exploration and possibly contact with any hypothetical entities/spirits/etc on that or any other celestial bodies, what could result in a game where tradition mages support strange spirits, dreaming exiles or whatever inhabiting Mars into conducting a supernatural guerilla &amp; sabotage effort against technocratic expansionist designs on the planet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-29T17:13:35-07:00","id":1455768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LaughingGull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455764-mars-terraforming-versus-human-genetic-engineering?p=1455765#post1455765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are we assuming that Mars is, as the technocracy would have us believe, an uninhabitable rocky planet and not the shard realm of the sphere of forces?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes. Interesting that the undertaking requires a mastery of all forms of energy on a technological level. So, I would say it still is the realm of forces, only reshaped by the new Consensus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":". 09-04-2021, 12:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-29T19:48:34-07:00","id":1455779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455764-mars-terraforming-versus-human-genetic-engineering?p=1455766#post1455766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My thoughts on the matter at the moment:<br /> <br /> - Progenitors would definitely favor the &quot;adapting people to the enviroment&quot; path, though experimenting with self-sustaining enviromental changes through the use of mutated bacterial and/or fungal (among other organisms) might also be an option.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I think if you create a food-chain with mutated fungi and bacteria, the humans at the top of the chain would also have to be altered so they can eat, unless they are cyborgs who only need electricity. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455764-mars-terraforming-versus-human-genetic-engineering?p=1455766#post1455766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Syndicate might favor or oppose it depending if they want the more economically practical or an astronomically costly and neverending undertaking that might assure the jobs of countless peoples for generations - in fact these and more could lead to something on a broken base on the issue.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Syndicate is thinking about risk/reward, they might go with engineering humans to reduce costs, seeing the project as a very long term investment. The colony will need a planetary currency which would facilitate the use of Primal Utility for obtaining quintessence there. <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455764-mars-terraforming-versus-human-genetic-engineering?p=1455766#post1455766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Iteration X views might be similar to those of Progenitors in prefering to tailor the people to the enviroment - through cybernetics in their case, obviously, what should lead to competition with the Progenitors over what method is more suited to the situation, practical to the Conventions resources and so on.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>The Statisticians could inform the decision with Time Magick. <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455764-mars-terraforming-versus-human-genetic-engineering?p=1455766#post1455766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- The Void Engineers might either accept any support as long as it gets the boat forward - or have some specific knowledge of conditions, natural &amp; supernatural, in the red planet, that makes them opposed to the idea of &quot;geo\u200bformatting&quot; as a whole. So, an ironic broken base potential much like with the Syndicate, i guess.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I can just imagine the Progenitors and Iteration X (Marco-technicians) building a space ship with no funding. It runs on biofuel.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455764-mars-terraforming-versus-human-genetic-engineering?p=1455766#post1455766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- NWO.... no idea whatsoever, really.\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be an opportunity to sell their services to the Conventions who are investing resources in the project. Colonies have a tendency to break away, politically, declaring independence. The NWO can condition the minds of the colonists to never dream of such ideas. They might even work with the Progenitors to ensure the conditioning is passed on from one generation to the next through epigenetic memory. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455764-mars-terraforming-versus-human-genetic-engineering?p=1455766#post1455766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the Traditions going to Mars.... honestly, i don't see anyone beside the Etherites having an interest on this as a group. Too far from their respective paradigms and arenas.<br /> <br /> Correction - Dreamspeakers, Akashics, Choristers, Batinni and others with some interest in out-of-body experiences and spiritual vision quests might involve themselves with astral journeys in other worlds, what might led, if not to attempts at colonization, at least a degree of exploration and possibly contact with any hypothetical entities/spirits/etc on that or any other celestial bodies, what could result in a game where tradition mages support strange spirits, dreaming exiles or whatever inhabiting Mars into conducting a supernatural guerilla &amp; sabotage effort against technocratic expansionist designs on the planet.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Leaving your body behind is the third option that the Technocracy would never consider. Maybe the Syndicate, since it costs nothing. A Mars base being invaded by astral travelers makes for a good adventure. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-30T03:40:35-07:00","id":1455792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455764-mars-terraforming-versus-human-genetic-engineering?p=1455768#post1455768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes. Interesting that the undertaking requires a mastery of all forms of energy on a technological level. So, I would say it still is the ream of forces, only reshaped by the new Consensus.</div> </div> </div> </div>I asked because, in prior editions, the Traditions were already there. In particular, Doissetep was there and so, if it's still there, I can't imagine the Order of Hermes would want sleeper colonists right next door to one of their major chantries either way. In fact, expanding the consensus out to the rest of the solar system is likely the technocracy's main motivation in colonizing other planets.<br /> <br /> As for other traditions, I agree that the Etherites would be the main ones interested in the project but whether their plan is to change the planet or the colonists, or simply to inhabit the canals abandoned by an ancient Martian civilisation, will depend on the individual Etherite.<br /> <br /> I think the Dreamspeakers would actively oppose any plan as they've had enough of colonization already, and even if there are no physical inhabitants there are likely spirits who don't need to be disturbed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24383-laughinggull","name":"LaughingGull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24383_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-30T06:27:30-07:00","id":1455794,"title":"","content":"If the Traditions tried colonizing Mars, as it physically exists in the current dominant paradigm of the world (the red rocky expanse with robots examining the rocks), their efforts would face immense backlash. Colonizing the shard realms is much more doable for them.<br /> <br /> As for what the NWO would look for in colonizing mars, it's definitely on the great timetable of technological advancement, and it's good PR.<br /> <br /> &quot;If you don't believe in science / the status quo, just look at the results - colonists living peaceful and happy lives on the red planet. I'm going there on vacation next year.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Ecoterrorists? Just terrorists, please. We've proven we can tame any planet, and these troglodites are crying about a few ice caps. Let the grownups set the agenda I say, we've proven that our methods work.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T17:42:50-07:00","id":1455890,"title":"","content":"There's actually a third way to colonize Mars, albeit as an extension of the first: Para-terraforming.<br /> <br /> Which is to say, creating enclosed environments on Mars that are livable, and just expanding that until most of the planet's usable surface is enclosed. The whole &quot;live under pressurized domes&quot; model, except on a larger scale. That, or having everyone live in tunnels underground.<br /> <br /> This is a far more achievable process, that won't take millennia to play out. It's a matter of construction, not of slowly altering atmospheres (not to mention it doesn't require creating a worldwide magnetic field, the lack of which is the cause of Mars losing its atmosphere to solar wind in the first place). It's still a massive engineering project, except to a certain extent it's not. Rather, it could be a series of smaller projects that can be built on over time. You start by building a few small bases, perfect the technology needed to keep it all contained, then add onto those bases or built more.<br /> <br /> In this light, I imagine paraterraforming would be of great interest to Iteration X. Specifically the Macrotechnicians, for whom large engineering projects are their jam.<br /> <br /> Moreover, paraterraforming is not, as a rule, mutually exclusive to the other two methods of colonization. It's a closed environment, meaning it doesn't stop them from either terraforming in the traditional sense, or of modifying people to live in the original Martian environment. Obviously, you would still need to choose one or the other, but paraterraforming can be a concurrent project that doesn't hinder either. Indeed, it's a lot easier to terraform if you've got bases on Mars already, that can slowly release amounts of air. The only terraforming method that paraterraforming wouldn't be good with are the ones that involve nukes.<br /> <br /> Yes, there are serious talks about using nuclear explosions to facilitate terraforming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T18:27:11-07:00","id":1455979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LaughingGull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455764-mars-terraforming-versus-human-genetic-engineering?p=1455792#post1455792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I asked because, in prior editions, the Traditions were already there. In particular, Doissetep was there and so, if it's still there, I can't imagine the Order of Hermes would want sleeper colonists right next door to one of their major chantries either way. In fact, expanding the consensus out to the rest of the solar system is likely the technocracy's main motivation in colonizing other planets.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my own campaign, Chantries are not as immensely powerful as Doissetep, but there's no Avatar Storm. So, medium sized ones, by comparison, would be the largest in existence (I am mainly talking about the number and power of the Mages, not the structures). My impression is that the writers thought they had made Chantries too powerful and required a dramatic destruction to scale things down. <br /> <br /> On a planet the size of Mars, &quot;right next door&quot; is unlikely. If the Technocracy are arriving on a planet where the Traditions have established themselves, they would start at some distance, so they could gather resources needed to eventually assail Tradition Chantries. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LaughingGull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455764-mars-terraforming-versus-human-genetic-engineering?p=1455792#post1455792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for other traditions, I agree that the Etherites would be the main ones interested in the project but whether their plan is to change the planet or the colonists, or simply to inhabit the canals abandoned by an ancient Martian civilisation, will depend on the individual Etherite.<br /> <br /> I think the Dreamspeakers would actively oppose any plan as they've had enough of colonization already, and even if there are no physical inhabitants there are likely spirits who don't need to be disturbed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some good intrigue possibilities if the Dreamspeakers find some Technomancers also opposed and make an alliance on that basis, possibly pushing the Etherites and the Technocratic colonies together.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455764-mars-terraforming-versus-human-genetic-engineering?p=1455794#post1455794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Traditions tried colonizing Mars, as it physically exists in the current dominant paradigm of the world (the red rocky expanse with robots examining the rocks), their efforts would face immense backlash. Colonizing the shard realms is much more doable for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Places in the Umbra appear different based on the beliefs of different travelers. <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455764-mars-terraforming-versus-human-genetic-engineering?p=1455794#post1455794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for what the NWO would look for in colonizing mars, it's definitely on the great timetable of technological advancement, and it's good PR.<br /> <br /> &quot;If you don't believe in science / the status quo, just look at the results - colonists living peaceful and happy lives on the red planet. I'm going there on vacation next year.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Ecoterrorists? Just terrorists, please. We've proven we can tame any planet, and these troglodites are crying about a few ice caps. Let the grownups set the agenda I say, we've proven that our methods work.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>So, Syndicate - Media Control as well. Helps heal the rift between the two Conventions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455764-mars-terraforming-versus-human-genetic-engineering?p=1455890#post1455890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's actually a third way to colonize Mars, albeit as an extension of the first: Para-terraforming.<br /> <br /> Which is to say, creating enclosed environments on Mars that are livable, and just expanding that until most of the planet's usable surface is enclosed. The whole &quot;live under pressurized domes&quot; model, except on a larger scale. That, or having everyone live in tunnels underground.<br /> <br /> This is a far more achievable process, that won't take millennia to play out. It's a matter of construction, not of slowly altering atmospheres (not to mention it doesn't require creating a worldwide magnetic field, the lack of which is the cause of Mars losing its atmosphere to solar wind in the first place). It's still a massive engineering project, except to a certain extent it's not. Rather, it could be a series of smaller projects that can be built on over time. You start by building a few small bases, perfect the technology needed to keep it all contained, then add onto those bases or built more.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it is a lot easier to get microbes multiplying in the soil underneath you than in a vast thin atmosphere. Story-wise, it confines the action quite a bit, but I am sure I'll think of a way to expand the theater of adventure. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455764-mars-terraforming-versus-human-genetic-engineering?p=1455890#post1455890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this light, I imagine paraterraforming would be of great interest to Iteration X. Specifically the Macrotechnicians, for whom large engineering projects are their jam.</div> </div> </div> </div>That Methodology is a big part of my story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455764-mars-terraforming-versus-human-genetic-engineering?p=1455890#post1455890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moreover, paraterraforming is not, as a rule, mutually exclusive to the other two methods of colonization. It's a closed environment, meaning it doesn't stop them from either terraforming in the traditional sense, or of modifying people to live in the original Martian environment. Obviously, you would still need to choose one or the other, but paraterraforming can be a concurrent project that doesn't hinder either. Indeed, it's a lot easier to terraform if you've got bases on Mars already, that can slowly release amounts of air.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another purpose for a dome could be to focus a lot of light on an organism adapted to using all of it to grow. They would drill a hole, fill it with &quot;cheese&quot; - nutrients for the organism - and build the dome centered on the filled hole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455764-mars-terraforming-versus-human-genetic-engineering?p=1455890#post1455890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only terraforming method that paraterraforming wouldn't be good with are the ones that involve nukes.<br /> <br /> Yes, there are serious talks about using nuclear explosions to facilitate terraforming.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose that's on a planned timescale where the radiation would have time to dissipate. Might be some Barrabbi influence.<br /> ..<br /> <br /> Thank you all.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-03T05:20:53-07:00","id":1456067,"title":"","content":"Paraterraforming would work pretty well with nukes if the domes kept out the fallout and the ground was cleaned before the dome was extended. The water would have to be filtered as well if the domes are bringing it in from the outside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T04:35:00-07:00","id":1456410,"title":"","content":"The latter modifications would be too extreme, and isn't exactly likely to attract sleepers to the possibility of mars colonies. Terraforming is a humongous project, but it also has the advantage of, well, making the place more than just a low gravity dirt trail. As for the enclosure most people have suggested; far more feasible, but what would make you want to cross the cosmos to live in a what is at most Vegas in a bubble. Only if earth rapidly goes to shit, or wonderful economic incentives show up, does a mars bubble make sense.<br /> <br /> From most points of view, going to mars is a vanity project. But I suppose mages are... exceptionally driven people who don't like being told &quot;no&quot;. <br /> Even with magic, I think adaptations without some degree of terraforming is a waste","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T15:43:04-07:00","id":1456463,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure genetic engineering would work - or at least not in such a way that wouldn't require ignoring Consensus. You might do it with surgical or bionic alterations (ability to survive the colder temps, the radiation, the lowered pressures, the degradation from reduced gravity, the thin atmosphere, etc.) which also strikes me as mostly an Iteration X and/or Progentiors thing, although I suppose if you invoke sufficiently obscure nanotech handwavi-ness you could get away with something that looks/behaves more human outwardly. I'm also not certain that Martians would function well off the planet (again differences in pressure, gravity, etc.) without some sort of assistance. Mind you this idea isn't wholly inconsistent with the others (and as I mention below, the idea of 'altered' humans could play on some pulp sci fi concepts that might appeal.) <br /> <br /> Terraforming seems like a better option (its more sustainable for one thing and it might be friendlier on consensus from a handwaving perspective) but I also think the Union would want to avoid detection from earth or elsewhere (and signs of habitation could be detected in various ways if precautions aren't taken.) Part of me thinks that if they were going to terraform in some fashion they might go for a subterranean habitation that is more self-sustaining and avoids alot of the aforementioned problems. I'm also pretty sure that alot of older pulp sci fi featured underground martian civilizations.<br /> <br /> Artificial environments are another possibility, and possibly easier than terraforming something more self-sustaining but could backfire if things go wrong (the environment would still be hostile, after all.) <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-28T21:22:19-07:00","id":1457951,"title":"","content":"Scientifically speaking:<br /> <br /> Terraforming isn't feasible. Despite being actively researched, even in a best case scenario it would be a thousands of years undertaking under current scientific understanding. The problem is the sheer amount of additional matter and energy to make it and kickstart a new climate cycle. Altering humans to live under common Martian conditions indefinitely isn't feasible, either, it lacks fundamental conditions for life. Covering the entire planet in domes is actually worse than Terraforming it, instead of initiating a process you're going to make a planet-size building?<br /> <br /> From a practical perspective those options are thought exercises more than anything else for the foreseeable future. But building there in small scale is doable and more than enough for a colony (seriously, even for the entire human race, we're many, but on a planet scale not THAT many), so establishing a city isn't too much of a stretch. The major problem would be acclimating to low gravity, so curiously genetic engineering would still be necessary.<br /> <br /> And since there is still much to be learned from Mars, no scientist really wants to make any of this in too large a scale, anyways.<br /> <br /> Now, from Mages' perspectives:<br /> <br /> - The Technocratic Union would want to establish research colonies in a model similar to the one stated above, so to not stretch too much the Consensus. Those colonies would have some Enlightened Science, but would mainly serve as the next step in the Pogrom;<br /> <br /> - Astral travelers of several Traditions would want to secure colonies to help them protect their interests on Martian soil, that would probably boil down to preservation;<br /> <br /> - Other Traditions would be likely to develop an interest in Mars when the travels begin in earnest, to explore, develop more their Paradigms and establish strategical positions;<br /> <br /> - Etherites will try to Terraform anyway.<br /> <br /> One important factor to keep in mind is the ease to establish a local Paradigm when far from big population centers. Mars is as far as it gets. Be prepared for colonies that completely ignore things like air pressurization, preferring to breath the healthy Martian air, and actually being healthy that way.<br /> <br /> Interactions may also change considerably depending on the situation on the colonies at a given time. Like an alliance between Progenitors and Dreamspeakers to fight the destructive secret drilling joint project between the Order of Hermes and the Syndicate.<br /> <br /> Mars is likely to be very similar to the overall situation in space beyond the first Horizon even when it slips to within the Consensus, the difference being using rules for the Material Realm instead of the Umbra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-30T21:23:04-07:00","id":1458102,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind that Mars has a more complex Umbral landscape than most of the planets, with only Earth outdoing it and only Venus rivaling it. It's explicitly stated in Infinite Tapestry that most of the creatures and environments featured in early science fiction make their abode in either the Penumbra or the Umbra; and the Traditions who visit Mars are more likely to interact with this aspect of Mars than with the cold, dead world that the Technocracy is likely going to deal with. Infinite Tapestry does its usual thing of pointing out that is an interesting place to visit, but don't try to live there. Depending on the story you want to tell, you might want to be a bit more lenient \u2014 say, by giving Etherites a Spirit technique that lets them set up bases in the Martian Penumbra that, when properly maintained, can stave off Disembodiment indefinitely. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, there are the Earthly Foundations (well, <i>Martian</i> Foundations) to consider: I suspect that even as far out as Mars, you don't get to shift the Reality Zone to the point that the Martian environment is hospitable; not without going into the Penumbra, as mentioned above. Ever since the divide between Etherspace and Conventional Space was pushed out beyond the opportunity of Mars (a process that probably started with the Void Engineer Tychoides at the start of the 20th century), the idea of a habitable colony on the material surface of Mars without substantial life support technology has been Vulgar and likely resistant to paradigm manipulation (that is, you don't get to make it Coincidental just by importing a bunch of colonists who have been indoctrinated to believe that the air on Mars is breathable, or more generally that the environment can support life). Prior to that, all of Mars was \u201csubmerged\u201d in the Umbra, and there <i>was</i> no cold, dead surface to visit, unless deliberate efforts were made to force a region to separate out its Conventional Space, as per a Procedure to that effect that can be found in the Void Engineers Revised Convention Book. <br /> <br /> But that's effectively ancient history now; since at least the 1950s, the Spatial Horizon has extended out to the Asteroid Belt, and the inner planets (Mars included) have had surfaces in Conventional Space that are hostile to life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-31T01:45:53-07:00","id":1458115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455764-mars-terraforming-versus-human-genetic-engineering?p=1458102#post1458102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the idea of a habitable colony on the material surface of Mars without substantial life support technology has been Vulgar and likely resistant to paradigm manipulation (that is, you don't get to make it Coincidental just by importing a bunch of colonists who have been indoctrinated to believe that the air on Mars is breathable, or more generally that the environment can support life)</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering all the shit that Reality Zones and Paradigm Manipulation can do on Earth itself, with all of humanity living here, why Mars wouldn't be more flexible for humans living there? A colony with its own Reality Zone wouldn't even be noticeable from Earth. Remember that it is smaller than Earth, but still an entire planet, and actually one with more solid surface thanks to our oceans.<br /> <br /> If every Tradition, Convention and Craft builds each a colony for 100,000 inhabitants it wouldn't still even scratch the surface of Mars and hardly be perceived by someone who didn't knew what to look for. They don't need to alter Mars on a large scale, ever, just their tiny portion of its environment.<br /> <br /> On the Umbral side, just to address this, depending on where in the Umbra you're traveling the fact that you experience things differently do not keep you from interacting with other people. That is how the Void Engineers frequently ally with Traditionalists against aliens in the far reaches of space. This is particularly true for the Penumbra, where two travelers with irreconcilable experiences can still see and interact with each other. Except when they don't because the game doesn't want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-31T04:41:24-07:00","id":1458126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455764-mars-terraforming-versus-human-genetic-engineering?p=1458115#post1458115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering all the shit that Reality Zones and Paradigm Manipulation can do on Earth itself, with all of humanity living here, why Mars wouldn't be more flexible for humans living there?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because <i>Earthly Foundations</i> (M20 pp.612\u2013613) are specifically <i>not</i> about what people believe, and in fact frequently stand <i>in spite of</i> what people believe. Granted, the text as written assumes that we're talking about Earth; but it's one small step to extend the same logic to outer space and other planets: the basic way that physical reality works isn't set by human belief. And in an environment where exposure to human beliefs is almost nil, this baseline state of reality dominates. (Victorian Mage even goes so far as to say that if a region is depopulated, it will gradually revert to its Earthly Foundations.)<br /> <br /> And just like the Earthly Foundations on Earth establish that some things are and remain Vulgar even when the locals believe otherwise, so too with their Martian counterparts. The issue isn't about having to overcome human beliefs; it's about having to overcome the fundamental laws of reality. Gravity isn't as strong on Mars as it is on Earth; but water still flows downhill, not uphill. And that remains true even if you indoctrinated your colonists into believing otherwise. Likewise with other aspects of the environment, such as how cold it is and the lack of breathable air. The existence of these \u201cMartian Foundations\u201d is the whole reason why the Technocracy needs to consider Terraforming the planet at all, instead of \u201cmerely\u201d Terranorming the colonists into believing that the Martian environment is hospitable. <br /> <br /> Remember that, at least as of Technocracy Reloaded, the Union can and does involve itself in the game of reality alteration; so Terraforming a patch of Mars can't be as easy as convincing your colonists that it has already been Terraformed. If such a thing was possible, the NWO at least would be tempted to do it: altering reality by altering peoples' minds is what they do. Instead, any such efforts will run counter to the Earthly Foundations and will be Vulgar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-31T06:07:09-07:00","id":1458130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455764-mars-terraforming-versus-human-genetic-engineering?p=1458115#post1458115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering all the shit that Reality Zones and Paradigm Manipulation can do on Earth itself, with all of humanity living here, why Mars wouldn't be more flexible for humans living there? A colony with its own Reality Zone wouldn't even be noticeable from Earth. Remember that it is smaller than Earth, but still an entire planet, and actually one with more solid surface thanks to our oceans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uncolonized Mars would likely count as a Primal Reality Zone, and those do promote certain ideas and reject others. What things they welcome and what they are hostile to probably depend a lot on the needs of the story and assumptions about what Mars is like, both physically and spiritually. Regardless, even if you are importing people to turn the area into a Colonized Reality Zone, you still have to go through a period of time where you overcome the rules of the Primal Reality. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-31T06:16:50-07:00","id":1458132,"title":"","content":"Right. So that raises the question, what determines what the primal reality of Mars is like? Not human belief.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-31T06:55:42-07:00","id":1458138,"title":"","content":"I can see a number of ways of handling that based on what the focus of the story is. My default explanation would be that it is determined in part by a sort of fundamental <i>character</i> and in part by the influence of its Umbral denizens. The fundamental character would likely be the product of Mars' creation, but much like Earth there is no set answer on how that happened. I would not consider Mars' Primal Reality the fundamental reality of the planet, just its starting point and the valence point which it will currently drift back to if it is abandoned.<br /> <br /> If I wanted to run a game more focused on exploration, Mars, much like pre Sorcerer's Crusade Earth, could be in a certain amount of flux. Distances could be unreliable and there might be places that are only reachable from some locations and not others. Mars might only seem lifeless to humans because human belief says the barren areas are the only ones that can be reached directly from Earth. If I were going this route, the Mars Climate Orbiter was not lost due to a mathematical error but because it hit something that wasn't supposed to be there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 08-31-2021, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-31T10:25:15-07:00","id":1458156,"title":"","content":"My main point is the variety of things happening. Breathable air was an example that can be extreme, but the main point is the same: Mars' environment wouldn't be uniform, and the presence of Mage lead colonies would alter things significantly.<br /> <br /> It's environment would be inhospitable, but not as inflexible to magic as Earth's. Without humans it is probable that many rules are naturally less strict, as Ramnesis exemplified. Building colonies would probably be feasible to every Tradition according to its own paradigm, even if not easy or completely safe.<br /> <br /> And with the practical limit on size of such colonies, it would be probable that most of them become Chantries. The environment around may suffer some changes, not as intense as my previous hyperbole, but still enough to make contact between colonies weird.<br /> <br /> That's to say nothing about Mars itself. Given that even on Earth we have bygones and weird stuff.<br /> <br /> By the way, the idea that breathable air, or any other particular condition is supported by Foundations is an assumption. Even the Earthly Foundations have quite some flexibility, and Mars isn't <i>devoid</i> of atmosphere, despite having less than 1% of our surface pressure, nor a completely alien composition. It lacks enough oxygen, but isn't directly poisonous (the trace amounts of carbon monoxide aren't enough to be a danger, the carbon dioxide can be used for oxygen production). So despite it being completely unbreathable for real, it's hard to say how much this would be a Foundation in Mage. Especially considering that it wouldn't make Mars a lot less dangerous as an alien planet-size wild desert.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-31T11:35:56-07:00","id":1458161,"title":"","content":"If you want the challenges that the technocracy faces in terraforming Mars to resemble the real world challenges in terraforming mars, they need to be Earthly Foundations. Because the biggest difference between a regular reality Zone and an Earthly Foundation is that the latter cannot be overridden by the consensus; not in anything short of a generational time frame, anyway.<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that infinite tapestry mentioned an etherite base on Mars that terraformed its surroundings. Ultimately, the Bradbury base failed, because having one patch of livable land surrounded by uninhabitable terrain was paradoxical and resulted in the base transitioning into the Umbra, where the crew Disembodied. <br /> <br /> Conversely, Mars was also where Doissetup(sp?) was located.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-31T15:47:28-07:00","id":1458186,"title":"","content":"Oh, but just to be clear, I don't said that the Technocracy will <b><u>face</u></b> the same challenges, I think they'll <b><u>pretend</u></b> the same challenge.<br /> <br /> Colonizing for colonizing, everyone that had any interest in the Umbral Mars is already there, have been for a while. I'm thinking about a new wave of colonization: as soon as the first group starts to colonize Conventional Space Mars, it will become a race for strategic positions.<br /> <br /> And today we're talking this under the lens of the current situation, with four countries keeping parallel observation of the planet and dates being set for manned missions. That means a Technocratic colony won't be there just for secret projects, but also to stir the Consensus (and maybe move Conventional Space even further).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-31T18:44:18-07:00","id":1458203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455764-mars-terraforming-versus-human-genetic-engineering?p=1458186#post1458186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, but just to be clear, I don't said that the Technocracy will <b><u>face</u></b> the same challenges, I think they'll <b><u>pretend</u></b> the same challenge.</div> </div> </div> </div>And there it is. \u201cscience is BS, because the Technocracy is lying to us.\u201d I cannot tell you how sick I am of that trope. It diminished science, and it dilutes the Technocracy by having them be not just ethically wrong, but also metaphysically wrong. <i>And</i> it means that they're <i>stupid</i>, because there are much more effective ways to exploit Mars than to pretend that it's a lifeless rock if it isn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T04:41:28-07:00","id":1458216,"title":"","content":"I get your point and don't totally disagree. In fact one of the things I like in the Awakening is its distancing from that BS. Unfortunately this is one of the setting premises anyway, despicable as it is, although I also diminish it in my games to make science more properly a thing to be recognized and to me most of the greatest scientific geniuses that changed the world <i><b>weren't</b></i> technomancers, or guided by Mages, just plain, old, people working and thinking through the mundane yet incredible mysteries of nature.<br /> <br /> But I have a different interpretation on this case that works better. The Technocracy isn't just being ineffective and Mars <b>is</b> mostly a lifeless rock. They are much more advanced technologically than the general public is, and for them to start doing colonies at this point they'll have the attention of the masses in mind. They can do a much better job with their real tech, and they will surely do a much better job than people realize, but they still have to maintain the facade to keep the leaking of new technology as prescribed in their timetables.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the other Mages ability to do shit with localized Consensus and/or coincidental magic isn't the same as saying science isn't a thing. Even the Earth Foundations only kick in at extremes, not at every turn of basic science. Obliterating a building is always vulgar, but obliterating a chair is fine, although science does not really care about the distinction, both should be impossible. Changing a person into a chair is vulgar, but changing their liver into a pig's liver isn't, because magic understands the person as a single Pattern, science don't.<br /> <br /> My personal take is that the Earth Foundations aren't just the baseline nature of things, but mostly the limit on what can be done with magic, and Consensus IS magic as much as any Mage's spell. An area with breathable air because its inhabitants believe so (assumed here just as an example, I'm just saying it can be done by the ST, not that it should necessarily) is pretty much an area under magical alteration. There IS a baseline and this baseline IS unbreathable air, and the Technocracy do chooses to not mess with this natural reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T06:47:35-07:00","id":1458223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455764-mars-terraforming-versus-human-genetic-engineering?p=1458216#post1458216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get your point and don't totally disagree. In fact one of the things I like in the Awakening is its distancing from that BS. Unfortunately this is one of the setting premises anyway, despicable as it is, although I also diminish it in my games to make science more properly a thing to be recognized and to me most of the greatest scientific geniuses that changed the world <i><b>weren't</b></i> technomancers, or guided by Mages, just plain, old, people working and thinking through the mundane yet incredible mysteries of nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>This tends to be my view on it as well, except that I don't think that that <i>is</i> one of the setting premises \u2014 or of it was, it was a first edition premise that the game developers have been moving away from throughout the development of the game. It strikes me as being the whole reason why Earthly Foundations were introduced into M20.<br /> <br /> Let me clarify my thoughts about Earthly Foundations. They are very much <i>not</i> the limit of what can be done with magick. They do not limit mages any more than any other aspect of Reality Zones limit mages. Magick does not become impossible, or even more difficult, because of an Earthly Foundation. What Earthly Foundations limit is the Consensus.<br /> <br /> The role of the Consensus in the game is to influence Reality Zones; and outside of Marauders, it is the <i>only</i> thing that can influence Reality Zones. <u>The Earthly Foundations are those aspects of a Reality Zone that are immune to the influence of the Consensus.</u> Nothing more, nothing less. Which, in turn, means that they are those aspects of reality that you cannot change by persuading people to believe otherwise.<br /> <br /> To me, what makes Technocrats Scientists is that they explore and build on the Earthly Foundations. They're not lying when they say that there are things that are objectively true, and they <i>do</i> strive to ground their technology in that truth. That doesn't excuse the things they <i>do</i> with that technology; but their science and technology itself is not a lie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-01-2021, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T07:22:50-07:00","id":1458225,"title":"","content":"When I said limit I was talking about <i>Vulgarity</i>, and in this my stance stands. The Earthly Foundations don't enforce equally all the baseline rules of reality. By its own definition in the book it cares a lot about scale, in a way nature doesn't. Matter ceasing to exist doesn't happen from the scale of an atom upwards, but Earthly Foundations only care if it is building-size. Tissue transmutation is equally impossible with a piece of liver, but Earthly Foundations only care if it is an entire individual.<br /> <br /> And the Technocracy wouldn't have as much a problem with RDs as they have if it was just Earthly Foundations, they would exclusively police Vulgarity <i>against the Earthly Foundations</i>, which isn't the case. They do have a definition for a desirable Consensus that is stricter than the Earthly Foundations (even if it isn't the same as the current Consensus, either).<br /> <br /> I otherwise agree with your opinions, but the Earthly Foundations pretty much aren't as encompassing. Alone they're not enough to define nature, and against magick they don't go that far. And even the book says very little on what are the precise limits. We know that gravity can't be inverted (without invoking Paradox), and that explosions can happen up to a point, but not be too big. Heck, it even theorizes that mundane phenomena can cause Paradox! So it isn't even really keeping the Consensus at bay, because it recognizes that nuclear weapons and huge factories are a part of it and yet they may be <i>freaking Vulgar effects causing loads of Paradox</i>.<br /> <br /> So I'm pretty sure that they're not meant to limit how things can get weird in a Zone, but just when Paradox should kick in regardless of players' justifications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T07:56:37-07:00","id":1458227,"title":"","content":"First, you're right that Reality Zones dictate Vulgarity. That's why I said that Earthly Foundations don't hinder mages <i>any more than any other aspect of a Reality Zone does</i>: of a Reality Zones says that something's Vulgar, it's Vulgar; and it doesn't matter if it's Vulgar because the Consensus says that it's Vulgar, or if it's Vulgar because an Earthly Foundation says that it's Vulgar. <br /> <br /> I also never said that it was <i>just</i> Earthly Foundations that the Technocracy is concerned with; I said that the Earthly Foundations are what Technocratic Science and Technology are <i>built on</i>. And this is in the book, under the Technocratic Reality Zones, where it says that those zones have been as wildly successful as they have in part because they're based on the laws of physics \u2014 which pairs nicely with how Earthly Foundations says that any overt violation of the laws of physics is always Vulgar. <br /> <br /> And no, there's nothing in the books about mundane phenomena being able to cause Paradox. Magickal Effects that produce the equivalent of a nuclear blast cause Paradox; mundane nuclear warheads, if they exist, don't. Paradox is a phenomenon that's utterly unique to Magick, and does not exist apart from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T08:04:38-07:00","id":1458228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455764-mars-terraforming-versus-human-genetic-engineering?p=1458223#post1458223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, what makes Technocrats Scientists is that they explore and build on the Earthly Foundations. They're not lying when they say that there are things that are objectively true, and they <i>do</i> strive to ground their technology in that truth. That doesn't excuse the things they <i>do</i> with that technology; but their science and technology itself is not a lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I agree that the Technocracy's paradigms are based more firmly on the more stable points of reality than any of the Traditions. Is there something specific you are thinking of?<br /> <br /> Perhaps the issue is that I don't think things like Coulomb's Law or the Bernoulli Principle are deeply entrenched enough to even approach the level of an EF. Mythic threads perhaps, but not EFs.<br /> <br /> The Technocrats are scientists because they push a coherent, consistent, naturalistic*, and universal** paradigm. They do not use the scientific method as we understand it but that's more because the world of Mage makes that nigh impossible. They do, however, study those things that seem to be more reliably true, advance their understanding through iterative and empirical research, and seek to find and disseminate universally applicable principles. That such activities shore up reality in the way they want is not an accident, but neither does it invalidate their research and methodology.<br /> <br /> *historically, naturalism is not a necessary part of science, but it is closely associated with modern science.<br /> <br /> **that is, usable by everyone, at least eventually<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T08:27:10-07:00","id":1458230,"title":"","content":"I agree that things like Coulomb's law and the Bernoulli principle are not themselves Earthly Foundations. But they are based on Earthly Foundations. That is, they are designed to be fully consistent with the Earthly Foundations. That's what makes Enlightened Science naturalistic. Meanwhile, as I see it, the thing that makes it universal (to the extent that it is) is that they put in the effort to make it so; it isn't an automatic feature, but is something that they have worked to include. And for all the bad things that they have done, that is their single biggest redeeming quality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-01-2021, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T09:14:36-07:00","id":1458231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455764-mars-terraforming-versus-human-genetic-engineering?p=1458230#post1458230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that things like Coulomb's law and the Bernoulli principle are not themselves Earthly Foundations. But they are based on Earthly Foundations. That is, they are designed to be fully consistent with the Earthly Foundations. That's what makes Enlightened Science naturalistic.</div> </div> </div> </div>But what about those principles makes them consistent with the EFs when Traditionalist ones are not? I mean presumably Bernoulli's principle works well with the EFs of gravity and the existence of gas. The first is commonly listed as an EF and the second one plausibly could be. Yet it doesn't seem uniquely well suited. How are airplane wings working with those EFs better than any of the classic magical methods?<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, it is plausible and it works well as a setting element if that is what you need for a game. It just doesn't seem like an obvious or inevitable part of Mage's setting or metaphysics to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Meanwhile, as I see it, the thing that makes it universal (to the extent that it is) is that they put in the effort to make it so; it isn't an automatic feature, but is something that they have worked to include. And for all the bad things that they have done, that is their single biggest redeeming quality. </div> </div> </div>Well I meant universality in the sense that everything they do is technically doable by anyone. That doesn't take effort it is just an automatic result of their paradigm being based on external, natural principles. Since everything they do is based on those principles, anyone can do it once they know how (and once it is in the consensus).<br /> <br /> Their efforts to get their ideas into the consensus in usable and attractive ways does take effort, but it isn't the kind of universality I meant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T11:24:11-07:00","id":1458241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455764-mars-terraforming-versus-human-genetic-engineering?p=1458231#post1458231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what about those principles makes them consistent with the EFs when Traditionalist ones are not? I mean presumably Bernoulli's principle works well with the EFs of gravity and the existence of gas. The first is commonly listed as an EF and the second one plausibly could be. Yet it doesn't seem uniquely well suited. How are airplane wings working with those EFs better than any of the classic magical methods?<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, it is plausible and it works well as a setting element if that is what you need for a game. It just doesn't seem like an obvious or inevitable part of Mage's setting or metaphysics to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>M20, p.613:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Throughout our world in this 21<sup>st</sup> century, the Technocratic vision of reality holds the coincidental edge, <u>not simply because of the Union's indoctrination</u> (although that <i>does</i> have something to do with it) but because <u>science-based technology is rooted in following the laws of Earthly physics.</u> Unlike faith and magic, it's based upon repeatable, verifiable, consistent results, not mere Enlightened Will, so it tends to work more reliably than mystic magick does.</div>And the second bullet point for things that are violations of Earthly Foundations is \u201cObvious violations of normal physical laws\u201d. <br /> <br /> So physics is objectively a thing in M20, and science does a better job of making use of it than mysticism does. Not just my started preference; fact. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455764-mars-terraforming-versus-human-genetic-engineering?p=1458231#post1458231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I meant universality in the sense that everything they do is technically doable by anyone. That doesn't take effort it is just an automatic result of their paradigm being based on external, natural principles. Since everything they do is based on those principles, anyone can do it once they know how (and once it is in the consensus).<br /> <br /> Their efforts to get their ideas into the consensus in usable and attractive ways does take effort, but it isn't the kind of universality I meant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. And that's part of why I agree with you that Enlightened Science isn't <i>just</i> Earthly Foundations; there's a whole superstructure that's built on top of those Foundations, and that's super structure isn't universal in the same way that the Earthly foundations are because it does have to be pushed into the consensus before \u201canyone can use it\u201d. By contrast, Earthly foundations can be used by anyone even if the consensus actively rejects them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-01-2021, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T13:00:35-07:00","id":1458248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455764-mars-terraforming-versus-human-genetic-engineering?p=1458241#post1458241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">M20, p.613:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Throughout our world in this 21<sup>st</sup> century, the Technocratic vision of reality holds the coincidental edge, not simply because of the Union's indoctrination (although that <i>does</i> have something to do with it) but because <u>science-based technology is rooted in following the laws of Earthly physics.</u> Unlike faith and magic, it's based upon repeatable, verifiable, consistent results, not mere Enlightened Will, so it tends to work more reliably than mystic magick does.</div>And the second bullet point for things that are violations of Earthly Foundations is \u201cObvious violations of normal physical laws\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't read this section as the Technocracy rooting its work in the Earthly Foundations, for several reasons. Firstly because the suggested list of normal physical laws is so thin. The bullet point you mention has three:<br /> <br /> 1) Water not flowing uphill, which I presume is just gravity since it is actually trivial to make water flow upwards using real world physical laws.<br /> <br /> 2) Sudden apparition.<br /> <br /> 3) Turtles not running really fast, which I presume is a proscription against sudden acceleration since turtle speed would be an oddly specific EF. <br /> <br /> That's not a list that encompasses basic physics. It's barely enough to make a Christopher Nolan movie paradoxical. Clearly there can be more than are just listed here, but there don't have to be. They are also very general, they only specify that something generally happens or does not happen, they don't say how or why.<br /> <br /> That's important because when we think laws of physics we are usually thinking of things that are considerably more numerous and specific: thermal expansion, equal and opposite reactions, Bernoulli's principle, etc. Those aren't EFs, though. They are the hows to the EF's whats. They are either mythic (technic?) threads or technocratic (and pretechnocratic) principles. <br /> <br /> I certainly agree that the Technocracy is making it's principles consistent with those three ideas (and any others that may exist). So is everyone else. The witch having a demon move her broom, the sorcerer enchanting his carpet, and the engineer designing his wing and engine system are all doing the exact same thing: recognizing that things fall and carving out an exception why this time they don't.<br /> <br /> I certainly agree that the Technocracy is having a better time getting people to agree with their particular style of carving out exceptions, but their success doesn't seem to have anything to do with the suggested EFs. Indeed if I had to point out the elements that make them successful it would be the indoctrination and the reliable results. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T13:32:37-07:00","id":1458251,"title":"","content":"No comments about the first part of my post? The one where I quoted a section of the book where it has science contrasted with magic and faith, explicitly saying that the technocracy gets the coincidental edge in part because it's rooted in science? And that science is based upon repeatable, verifiable, and consistent results, whereas faith and magic are just Enlightened Will? Does that have no weight?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T14:23:58-07:00","id":1458255,"title":"","content":"You mean the one I quoted and made references to? Yes, I was looking at it. I was saying I don\u2019t think the technocratic reality zones reference to earthly physics can be interpreted as purely or even mostly as a reference EFs and I was using the physical law EF section to show why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 09-01-2021, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T15:08:40-07:00","id":1458262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455764-mars-terraforming-versus-human-genetic-engineering?p=1458227#post1458227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And no, there's nothing in the books about mundane phenomena being able to cause Paradox. Magickal Effects that produce the equivalent of a nuclear blast cause Paradox; mundane nuclear warheads, if they exist, don't. Paradox is a phenomenon that's utterly unique to Magick, and does not exist apart from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>M20, page 612, directly under Earthly Foundations:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M20,pp.612</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Sudden Large Alterations of Physical and Metaphysical<br /> Mass or Space: Stacking places on top of one another,<br /> disintegrating large structures, changing large masses<br /> of physical matter into large emissions of energy (i.e.,<br /> explosions), radical transformations of one physical<br /> form into another (that is, people into stone or vampires<br /> into lawn chairs)... such things disrupt Reality on a<br /> fundamental level. <b>Even when performed by technology,<br /> such large-scale alterations are never truly safe. <u>The<br /> horrific consequences of nuclear detonation could<br /> be seen as manifestations of the Paradox Effect; so<br /> could environmental pollution, climate change, organ<br /> rejection, electromagnetic pulses, cancer, and other<br /> aftershocks of technological disruption</u>. The bigger the<br /> Effect, the larger the consequences...</b> and no matter who<br /> you are or how you work your magicks, no mage acts<br /> without consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that is more of an aside. I think you read more in the Earthly Foundations than there really is, mashing two concepts that aren't equal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T16:36:01-07:00","id":1458271,"title":"","content":"And I think that you're not seeing what is there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T06:10:06-07:00","id":1458328,"title":"","content":"Let me clarify, as it sounds like what I was saying might have been unclear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455764-mars-terraforming-versus-human-genetic-engineering?p=1458241#post1458241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">M20, p.613:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Throughout our world in this 21<sup>st</sup> century, the Technocratic vision of reality holds the coincidental edge, <u>not simply because of the Union's indoctrination</u> (although that <i>does</i> have something to do with it) but because <u>science-based technology is rooted in following the laws of Earthly physics.</u> Unlike faith and magic, it's based upon repeatable, verifiable, consistent results, not mere Enlightened Will, so it tends to work more reliably than mystic magick does.</div>And the second bullet point for things that are violations of Earthly Foundations is \u201cObvious violations of normal physical laws\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>It looks to me like you are pointing to the underlined section as your strongest reason for why the Technocracy is rooted in Earthly Foundations. Specifically you are interpreting the reference to earthly physics as a reference to EFs and specifically to the kind listed in the &quot;obvious violations of normal physical laws&quot; section. Now the way I see it, there are a few ways of reading the part you underlined:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">1) There is the way you are interpreting it: &quot;Earthly physics&quot; is a reference to Earthly Foundations. <br /> <br /> 2) The underlined part isn't referring to EFs, it is referring to the more detailed physical laws that people are familiar with. These are quite solidly entrenched in reality, but not at anything like an EF level. <br /> <br /> 3) &quot;Earthly physics&quot; are a technocracy party line that they've managed to convince most of the world of. The Technocracy isn't playing better with reality, it is playing better with the reality it has convinced people of. Not my favorite view, but definitely one I've seen.</div> <br /> My previous post was largely an explanation of why I can't agree with interpretation 1. The EFs are too general to lend themselves to a specific type of paradigm. Certainly the Technocracy is accounting for them but so is everyone else. We can, of course, just say that the Technocracy is better at it, but there's no indication of how so that seems arbitrary. We could also shore this one up by assuming more specific and numerous physical EFs, but I'm not going to do that without compelling reason.<br /> <br /> I don't like number 3 either. While I do think the Technocracy would still claim to be using earthly physics even if they were knowingly making it up whole cloth, it doesn't match the kind of research and development methodology they pursue. It also isn't an edge, and I presume that the three things listed (indoctrination, rooted in physics, and results) are all supposed to be edges. <br /> <br /> It's the second interpretation that makes the most sense to me. It fits the Technocracy's approach and gives them a firm foundation. Other factions will have similarly entrenched foundations, true, but that's where the Technocracy's other two edges come into play. It also happens to play best with the section on Deep Wilderness and failing technology. This is the one that fits what I know of Mage and the Technocracy best and requires the fewest assumptions to make it work.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T06:55:36-07:00","id":1458338,"title":"","content":"And the third interpretation is also in direct violation of the first part that I underlined, which explicitly says that the Union's coincidental edge <i>isn't</i> solely due to indoctrination, which is what \u201ca technocracy party line that they've managed to convince most of the world of\u201d would be. Likewise with the notion that the bulk of the laws of physics were <i>invented by</i> the Technocracy: the only way for something invented to become part of a Reality Zone is through the Consensus (changes imposed by Marauders don't stick, thankfully), and that requires something to the effect of indoctrination. <br /> <br /> But yeah, I can get behind the notion that some or all of the laws of physics are in fact part of Primal Reality, which I interpret as \u201cReality that's untouched by the Consensus\u201d \u2014 though that tends to contradict the description in M20, which tends to be more about hostility to Technocratic Reality than anything else. I've implicitly been using \u201cEarthly Foundations\u201d when referring to a whole Reality Zone in this way; but that's not correct, either. Hmm\u2026<br /> <br /> Anyway, back to the subject of Mars: <i>whatever</i> you call a Reality Zone that's untouched by the Consensus, that's what you'll find on the material surface of Mars \u2014 unless you consider photos from an orbiting map-maker satellite to be \u201ctouched by the Consensus\u201d, in which case it's likely to lean more toward Technocratic Reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T08:44:30-07:00","id":1458358,"title":"","content":"There's definitely a bit of hazy terminology in the Reality Zones. Sometimes Primal Reality is just the non-technocrat equivalent of Technocratic Reality, and I think we should consider that a part of some other grouping. Other times it earth in a closer to 'natural' state, or beholden to some ancient power, or an otherworldly place. For the purposes of our previous conversation, yes, I think the Technocracy would definitely try to identify and build on the more naturalistic elements of the real Primal Reality Zones. Various factions may seek out the others, but outside of the OoH I don't know that many would hunt them diligently.<br /> <br /> As for Mars, we have to decide if the Martian surface is Deep Wilderness or a kind of Otherworld. Deep Wilderness is the most likely but Earth's Deep Wildernesses tend to be hostile to technology like the rovers. Either Martian Deep Wilderness is more open, or the 'Old Ways' of Mars are compatible with technology, or somehow parts of Mars have already been converted to something else.<br /> <br /> Mars as an Otherworld or series of Otherworlds would work, but leaves it entirely up to the ST how to define that. There's an opportunity for a kind of mystic wild west here, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 09-02-2021, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T09:37:20-07:00","id":1458366,"title":"","content":"It's been established that Mars has a \u201cSpirit Wilds\u201d Umbra, and that it's populated with the sorts of aliens seen in early science fiction (Barsoom, Malachandra, Wells' War of the Worlds \u2014 although there's also a suggestion that there might be a Hollow Mars, and I'd be inclined to put the latter there). That gives us a place for everything.<br /> <br /> My thought on this also has to do with the nature and development of science fiction stories pertaining to Mars: as late as the 1930s, Mars tended to be depicted as a more or less habitable and inhabited world; this tends to coincide with the idea that the spatial horizon had not yet been extended out that far, and there was no distinct physical Mars to visit; so all such visits were to the Martian spirit wilds. As the spatial horizon extended out to mars, started to get story of a more desolate planet, still inhabited by Martians living underground; this is where you get things like Ray Bradbury's Martian Chronicles. Then, after the pioneer mission, all pretenses of Mars being inhabited than it, and subsequent stories almost exclusively deal with uninhabited physical surface.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-02-2021, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T08:17:24-07:00","id":1458522,"title":"","content":"I do like the approach of Mars being its own thing rather than a reflection of Earth's fiction. The Spirit Wilds part also fits in well with how I tend to think of irreconcilable but strongly entrenched reality zones interacting. The one question is does this allow for the possibility that Martian beliefs impact the consensus or not?<br /> <br /> I don't remember exactly how other planets' umbrae work, but it seems to me that it would be very easy to reconcile the Martians having a consensus if they existed in a Horizon or Parallel Dimension style realm, but much harder if they were now a kind of High Umbral realm. I'd have to check my books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 09-03-2021, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T09:29:17-07:00","id":1458533,"title":"","content":"A Consensus comes from the population having Sleeping Avatars, something that spirits lack. So the question is whether or not you want your Martians too be capable of Awakening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T10:42:30-07:00","id":1458540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455764-mars-terraforming-versus-human-genetic-engineering?p=1458533#post1458533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Consensus comes from the population having Sleeping Avatars, something that spirits lack. So the question is whether or not you want your Martians too be capable of Awakening.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's my concern, yes. If Martians exist I prefer them to have equal worth and impact as humans. It's not necessary for all stories, but it is for many of the stories I would tell with them. Metaphysically that includes having Avatars (or at least the potential for them) and an impact on the Consensus. Not only does that mean they can't start as spirits, but I also don't think the human consensus could shunt the Martian consensus into the umbra. More likely something would happen to make it impossible to get from one civilization to the other through conventional means.<br /> <br /> In my (semi) headcanon that's something that already happened as Earth was mapped out. I believe Sorcerer's Crusade makes mention of areas that could only sometimes be reached. As things solidified I think some became places that could never be reached. That doesn't mean they were ejected into the Umbra, there just wasn't a physical path anymore. That's one way I would approach the exploration of Mars.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T11:11:02-07:00","id":1458545,"title":"","content":"Victorian mage, actually. There's a section about how technocratic cartography is used to map a number of Earthly locations into the Umbra. I'm pretty sure that it's more than a consensus versus consensus thing; it's Enlightened Science.<br /> <br /> (It's Enlightened Science that I'm not comfortable with, mind you. The map is not the territory in the technocratic paradigm. I could see the order of Hermes pulling off that stunt; but it doesn't strike me as appropriate for the technocracy.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T12:13:22-07:00","id":1458555,"title":"","content":"I haven't read Victorian Mage, though I need to. I know Sorcerer's Crusade made mention of distances and paths not always being the same. I thought there was something in there about paths not always existing, but I may have just extrapolated that.<br /> <br /> I should say that I don't have a problem using Umbral Realms as locations for alternate Earths, Mars, or whatever. Plenty of Umbral Realms have their own penumbra, their own rules, etc. I don't mind saying &quot;these spirits are special&quot; for a game if I need to. That said, the idea of aliens with avatars seems reasonable enough that I'd rather account for them more consistently. Alternate physical worlds hidden in the Umbra and Everett Volumes sounds more appropriate for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}